00:21:49.830 --> 00:21:52.080
of a hypersonic missile system,

00:21:52.080 --> 00:21:53.340
technology that would allow it

00:21:53.340 --> 00:21:56.310
to fire a nuclear warhead
faster than anyone else.

00:21:56.310 --> 00:21:58.770
- The US does not
currently have the ability

00:21:58.770 --> 00:22:01.803
to even track this weapon,
much less defeat it.

00:22:03.540 --> 00:22:05.670
- US military generals wake up one morning

00:22:05.670 --> 00:22:09.030
to discover that China has
just tested a new weapon,

00:22:09.030 --> 00:22:11.482
a missile that flew
around the entire world,

00:22:11.482 --> 00:22:14.753
going five times the speed
of sound, a mile a second.

00:22:14.753 --> 00:22:16.020
Oh, and it's really hard to see

00:22:16.020 --> 00:22:18.150
because it flies below radar range.

00:22:18.150 --> 00:22:19.950
It's super nimble, maneuverable,

00:22:19.950 --> 00:22:21.578
and has the ability to carry nukes.

00:22:21.578 --> 00:22:23.910
The US had been working
on something similar,

00:22:23.910 --> 00:22:26.602
but China beat them to it by years

00:22:26.602 --> 00:22:29.352
and it was American microchip technology

00:22:29.352 --> 00:22:31.203
that helped them build it.

00:22:32.729 --> 00:22:35.550
Oh shit.

00:22:35.550 --> 00:22:37.230
Yikes.

00:22:37.230 --> 00:22:38.970
This totally caught them off guard.

00:22:38.970 --> 00:22:42.120
- [Narrator] Says that US
intelligence services had no idea

00:22:42.120 --> 00:22:43.830
that China was so far ahead.

00:22:43.830 --> 00:22:45.450
- So turns out that while
the US government thought

00:22:45.450 --> 00:22:48.000
that they were running faster
and that they were fine,

00:22:48.000 --> 00:22:50.340
they were actually fueling the
rise of their biggest rival

00:22:50.340 --> 00:22:53.700
by giving them the technology
that they need to get ahead.

00:22:53.700 --> 00:22:56.056
So the US decides that
they've gotta do something.

00:22:56.056 --> 00:22:58.583
China is ahead on these missiles
and they might get ahead

00:22:58.583 --> 00:23:01.920
on things like AI and they're
doing it with our tech.

00:23:01.920 --> 00:23:04.725
No more free trade, no more free markets.

00:23:04.725 --> 00:23:07.307
The government is jumping
back into the chip game

00:23:07.307 --> 00:23:08.790
to sort this out.

00:23:08.790 --> 00:23:11.160
- Fundamental change
is taking place today,

00:23:11.160 --> 00:23:13.620
politically, economically,
and technologically.

00:23:13.620 --> 00:23:15.870
- All right, Joe Biden's
like rolling up his sleeves.

00:23:15.870 --> 00:23:16.740
He's like, what do we do here?

00:23:16.740 --> 00:23:19.920
Step one, cut 'em off,
no more chips for China.

00:23:19.920 --> 00:23:22.260
- The Biden administration
published a large set

00:23:22.260 --> 00:23:24.480
of export controls on Friday in order

00:23:24.480 --> 00:23:28.140
to slow Beijing's technological
and military advances.

00:23:28.140 --> 00:23:31.020
- [Speaker] Restrictions will
limit Chinese companies access

00:23:31.020 --> 00:23:32.403
to advanced computer chip.

00:23:36.420 --> 00:23:39.600
- And here we are, back in the
fun, bureaucratic paperwork,

00:23:39.600 --> 00:23:42.960
Department of Commerce, Bureau
of Industry and Security,

00:23:42.960 --> 00:23:46.730
docket number 220930-0204RIN0674...

00:23:50.947 --> 00:23:52.320
"Certain advanced computing

00:23:52.320 --> 00:23:55.110
and semiconductor manufacturing
items, supercomputers,

00:23:55.110 --> 00:23:58.241
and semiconductor end use,
entity list modification."

00:23:58.241 --> 00:24:00.060
We're not gonna go through this.

00:24:00.060 --> 00:24:02.010
This is just a bunch of rules

00:24:02.010 --> 00:24:04.140
that says no more chips to China.

00:24:04.140 --> 00:24:06.480
All those cutting edge
chips that China was buying

00:24:06.480 --> 00:24:08.070
from US companies, blocked.

00:24:08.070 --> 00:24:10.085
- [Speaker] The restrictions
will limit Chinese companies

00:24:10.085 --> 00:24:12.240
access to advanced computer chips.

00:24:12.240 --> 00:24:13.440
- [Speaker] Manufacturing
equipment they need

00:24:13.440 --> 00:24:14.700
to make their own chips?

00:24:14.700 --> 00:24:15.533
Blocked.

00:24:15.533 --> 00:24:18.840
All that US made vital software
that Chinese companies need

00:24:18.840 --> 00:24:20.160
to design their own chips?

00:24:20.160 --> 00:24:21.330
Blocked, blocked, blocked.

00:24:21.330 --> 00:24:24.390
- We will bring these
jobs back to our shores

00:24:24.390 --> 00:24:27.065
and end our dependence on foreign chips.

00:24:27.065 --> 00:24:28.020
- All right.

00:24:28.020 --> 00:24:28.853
- In fact,

00:24:28.853 --> 00:24:30.300
the Biden administration
went super far to say

00:24:30.300 --> 00:24:33.100
that any company globally
that uses US tech

00:24:33.100 --> 00:24:36.630
to produce chips is now
blocked from doing business

00:24:36.630 --> 00:24:37.890
with Chinese firms.

00:24:37.890 --> 00:24:39.210
- [Speaker] To cut China off from

00:24:39.210 --> 00:24:40.860
certain semiconductor chips made

00:24:40.860 --> 00:24:42.930
anywhere in the world with US equipment.

00:24:42.930 --> 00:24:43.830
- Why stop there?

00:24:43.830 --> 00:24:45.900
Americans are now forbidden from working

00:24:45.900 --> 00:24:49.290
for Chinese chip companies,
this is huge news.

00:24:49.290 --> 00:24:50.910
Like this is huge news, this is happening.

00:24:50.910 --> 00:24:53.190
This is like we're in the
middle of this right now.

00:24:53.190 --> 00:24:55.980
But let's go back to that visual
of the whole supply chain.

00:24:55.980 --> 00:24:58.848
If you cut off this, then
yeah, you hurt China,

00:24:58.848 --> 00:25:02.400
but you also hurt the
other side of this line,

00:25:02.400 --> 00:25:03.810
US chip makers.

00:25:03.810 --> 00:25:06.180
Like one example, this
US chipmaker, Nvidia,

00:25:06.180 --> 00:25:08.340
they went from selling
tons of chips to China

00:25:08.340 --> 00:25:10.530
to suddenly being banned from doing so.

00:25:10.530 --> 00:25:13.380
This has led to a $400
million loss in revenue

00:25:13.380 --> 00:25:14.790
in just one quarter.

00:25:14.790 --> 00:25:16.380
Poof, up in smoke.

00:25:16.380 --> 00:25:18.870
One of the biggest chip
makers now totally cut off

00:25:18.870 --> 00:25:23.160
from their big customer
because Joe Biden is afraid

00:25:23.160 --> 00:25:25.320
of the Chinese military
and for good reason,

00:25:25.320 --> 00:25:27.420
which leads to step two of this policy.

00:25:27.420 --> 00:25:28.560
The Biden administration
wasn't gonna leave

00:25:28.560 --> 00:25:29.910
these tech companies out dry.

00:25:29.910 --> 00:25:33.540
So they gave billions of
dollars to American chip makers

00:25:33.540 --> 00:25:35.640
to say, "Hey, yes, sorry we cut you off

00:25:35.640 --> 00:25:37.350
from your main customer because
we're kind of getting scared

00:25:37.350 --> 00:25:38.183
of their military,

00:25:38.183 --> 00:25:40.830
but we have to protect our
chips, here's a bunch of money."

00:25:40.830 --> 00:25:42.480
Congress passed the CHIPS Act,

00:25:42.480 --> 00:25:44.460
which gives billions of
dollars to these companies

00:25:44.460 --> 00:25:46.735
to create FABS back in the United States.

00:25:46.735 --> 00:25:50.280
- This time it wasn't Russia
but China, another rival power

00:25:50.280 --> 00:25:51.720
would get way ahead of us

00:25:51.720 --> 00:25:54.210
if we didn't pull out all the stops.

00:25:54.210 --> 00:25:58.350
And this legislation
is the first large step

00:25:58.350 --> 00:26:00.221
in pulling out all of those stops.

00:26:00.221 --> 00:26:02.712
- Government wants the
FABS to come home to ensure

00:26:02.712 --> 00:26:06.510
that this most valuable
technology isn't solely reliant

00:26:06.510 --> 00:26:09.480
on outside countries and
we're talking giant payouts.

00:26:09.480 --> 00:26:13.560
50 billion taxpayer dollars
go to companies like Intel,

00:26:13.560 --> 00:26:15.597
which is now opening a new FAB in Ohio.

00:26:15.597 --> 00:26:18.384
- We are gonna build the most
advanced stuff in the world,

00:26:18.384 --> 00:26:19.950
right here in Ohio.

00:26:19.950 --> 00:26:23.700
- Or even TSMC themselves,
which is based in Taiwan,

00:26:23.700 --> 00:26:26.730
but is now opening a new FAB in Arizona.

00:26:26.730 --> 00:26:27.870
Keep it in the family.

00:26:27.870 --> 00:26:30.750
Okay, so this is economic war
and the Biden administration

00:26:30.750 --> 00:26:32.340
just did a huge move.

00:26:32.340 --> 00:26:34.710
Reminder that the reason
why this is important is

00:26:34.710 --> 00:26:38.250
because it's not just about
like business or even missiles.

00:26:38.250 --> 00:26:40.020
This is about chips.

00:26:40.020 --> 00:26:42.720
Chips are not just chips,
chips are the future.

00:26:42.720 --> 00:26:43.860
Chips are power.

00:26:43.860 --> 00:26:47.280
Yes, chips mean economic
growth and new cool technology,

00:26:47.280 --> 00:26:49.440
but chips also mean new weapons.

00:26:49.440 --> 00:26:52.440
Chips are the currency
of geopolitical power,

00:26:52.440 --> 00:26:54.150
kind of like what oil used to be,

00:26:54.150 --> 00:26:55.654
but now it's freaking silicon with a bunch

00:26:55.654 --> 00:26:57.117
of on and off switches on it.

00:26:57.117 --> 00:26:59.970
The US is taking control
of its valuable resource

00:26:59.970 --> 00:27:01.320
and cutting China off.

00:27:01.320 --> 00:27:03.720
So the US makes this big
move, cuts China off,

00:27:03.720 --> 00:27:05.730
and this is geopolitical conflict.

00:27:05.730 --> 00:27:08.910
They just made the move, the
ball's in China's court now.

00:27:08.910 --> 00:27:10.200
How will they respond?

00:27:10.200 --> 00:27:13.447
And this is where Taiwan
comes back into the picture.

00:27:13.447 --> 00:27:16.114
(upbeat music)

00:27:17.700 --> 00:27:19.620
Taiwan is this small
country that finds itself

00:27:19.620 --> 00:27:21.510
in the crossfires of this conflict.

00:27:21.510 --> 00:27:25.170
92% of all advanced chips
are made here mostly by TSMC.

00:27:25.170 --> 00:27:27.360
The US is totally reliant on them.

00:27:27.360 --> 00:27:30.090
A few months before the Biden
administration was doing all

00:27:30.090 --> 00:27:32.820
of this, making it illegal
to sell chips to China,

00:27:32.820 --> 00:27:35.640
Congresswoman Nancy Pelosi visited Taiwan,

00:27:35.640 --> 00:27:38.479
not just to like shake hands
with political leaders, no,

00:27:38.479 --> 00:27:42.180
she was there to visit TSMC, the chip FAB.

00:27:42.180 --> 00:27:45.247
What Pelosi was really doing
here was signaling to Taiwan

00:27:45.247 --> 00:27:48.030
that they are vital to American security.

00:27:48.030 --> 00:27:50.340
US relies on this and will protect it.

00:27:50.340 --> 00:27:53.280
- Came to Taiwan to make
unequivocally clear,

00:27:53.280 --> 00:27:57.060
we'll not abandon our commitment
to Taiwan and we are proud

00:27:57.060 --> 00:27:58.500
of our enduring friendship.

00:27:58.500 --> 00:27:59.340
- And in doing so,

00:27:59.340 --> 00:28:02.040
she shows us what China's
counter move might be

00:28:02.040 --> 00:28:04.260
in all of this, it might be Taiwan.

00:28:04.260 --> 00:28:06.540
- Are you willing to
get involved militarily

00:28:06.540 --> 00:28:08.587
to defend Taiwan if it comes to that?

00:28:08.587 --> 00:28:10.590
- Yes, that's a commitment we made.

00:28:10.590 --> 00:28:11.423
- Okay, but wait,

00:28:11.423 --> 00:28:13.820
what this doesn't mean is like
China's gonna invade Taiwan

00:28:13.820 --> 00:28:16.476
and like take all the chips
or like take over the FAB

00:28:16.476 --> 00:28:18.630
or something, that that
scenario doesn't make any sense.

00:28:18.630 --> 00:28:20.220
If China invaded Taiwan,

00:28:20.220 --> 00:28:22.470
all they would find is
a bunch of empty FABS

00:28:22.470 --> 00:28:24.060
if they weren't bombed already.

00:28:24.060 --> 00:28:25.440
They wouldn't know how to operate them.

00:28:25.440 --> 00:28:28.170
They wouldn't have all of the
engineers and the software

00:28:28.170 --> 00:28:30.690
and all of the supply chain
stuff that they would need

00:28:30.690 --> 00:28:32.040
to actually make chips.

00:28:32.040 --> 00:28:34.320
They would likely be fighting a war

00:28:34.320 --> 00:28:36.090
and the US would probably get involved.

00:28:36.090 --> 00:28:37.500
I made a whole video about
it, you can go check it out.

00:28:37.500 --> 00:28:38.333
Anyway,

00:28:38.333 --> 00:28:40.500
the effective counter move
here for China would be

00:28:40.500 --> 00:28:43.800
to operate right on the
edge of active warfare

00:28:43.800 --> 00:28:44.940
to strike back at the US

00:28:44.940 --> 00:28:47.460
without provoking a military response.

00:28:47.460 --> 00:28:49.170
This is how big nuclear powers do it.

00:28:49.170 --> 00:28:50.250
They don't actually clash.

00:28:50.250 --> 00:28:52.020
They want to just sort
of poke at each other.

00:28:52.020 --> 00:28:54.000
One scenario would be
China sending a bunch

00:28:54.000 --> 00:28:57.210
of its navy ships to set up in
the ocean right around here,

00:28:57.210 --> 00:28:59.220
creating a kind of partial blockade.

00:28:59.220 --> 00:29:00.960
They could stop cargo
ships that are coming

00:29:00.960 --> 00:29:02.100
to and from the island,

00:29:02.100 --> 00:29:03.960
kind of just slowing everything down,

00:29:03.960 --> 00:29:06.480
but really holding the silicon hostage,

00:29:06.480 --> 00:29:09.344
making it hard for the supply
chain to actually work.

00:29:09.344 --> 00:29:12.870
I mean just remember like
the Covid 19 chip shortage

00:29:12.870 --> 00:29:14.010
or like supply chain shortage

00:29:14.010 --> 00:29:15.630
or even like the Suez Canal blockage

00:29:15.630 --> 00:29:16.920
from a couple years ago.

00:29:16.920 --> 00:29:19.790
Imagine those supply chain
issues, but like on steroids,

00:29:19.790 --> 00:29:23.790
totally debilitating and being
used for a hostile purpose

00:29:23.790 --> 00:29:25.260
to strike back at the US.

00:29:25.260 --> 00:29:27.510
Like Biden forbidding American companies

00:29:27.510 --> 00:29:28.620
to sell chips to China,

00:29:28.620 --> 00:29:30.510
the blockade would be a way to strike

00:29:30.510 --> 00:29:33.180
at your nuclear armed rival
without going too far,

00:29:33.180 --> 00:29:36.063
without risking too much
escalation or a miscalculation.

00:29:38.610 --> 00:29:40.740
- [Speaker] It's incumbent
upon us to stay number one.

00:29:40.740 --> 00:29:42.990
- [Speaker] To lead the
world in future industries,

00:29:42.990 --> 00:29:44.177
protect our national security.

00:29:44.177 --> 00:29:45.660
- [Speaker] We are gonna build the most

00:29:45.660 --> 00:29:47.370
advanced stuff in the world.

00:29:47.370 --> 00:29:48.203
- That's where we're at.

00:29:48.203 --> 00:29:49.980
We're in the middle of
another economic war

00:29:49.980 --> 00:29:51.990
between big nuclear powers.

00:29:51.990 --> 00:29:53.280
We don't know what happens next,

00:29:53.280 --> 00:29:55.950
but one thing that feels clear
to me is that Cold War vibes

00:29:55.950 --> 00:29:58.980
are back as these two great
powers with different ideologies

00:29:58.980 --> 00:30:00.870
about the world compete with each other.

00:30:00.870 --> 00:30:03.210
This fight over chips will continue.

00:30:03.210 --> 00:30:06.000
And this idea in international
relations that I kind of took

00:30:06.000 --> 00:30:06.833
for granted,

00:30:06.833 --> 00:30:09.090
which is that like globalization
and interdependence is good

00:30:09.090 --> 00:30:10.476
and will lead to less conflict,

00:30:10.476 --> 00:30:12.504
it's being seriously challenged.

00:30:12.504 --> 00:30:16.410
Economic interdependence
is being used as a weapon.

00:30:16.410 --> 00:30:18.030
That's what we're seeing
here and not just here.

00:30:18.030 --> 00:30:19.140
I made a video a couple months ago

00:30:19.140 --> 00:30:21.810
about how Vladimir Putin
is cutting off natural gas

00:30:21.810 --> 00:30:23.040
to Europe, frankly,

00:30:23.040 --> 00:30:25.830
it's not that much different
than Joe Biden cutting

00:30:25.830 --> 00:30:27.690
off microchips to China.

00:30:27.690 --> 00:30:29.340
I mean it is different in a
lot of ways, blah, blah, blah,

00:30:29.340 --> 00:30:30.173
we get it.

00:30:30.173 --> 00:30:31.170
But like the the big mechanics

00:30:31.170 --> 00:30:32.610
of how this conflict is playing out,

00:30:32.610 --> 00:30:34.560
it's peculiar and and is becoming a part

00:30:34.560 --> 00:30:35.940
of how conflict looks today.

00:30:35.940 --> 00:30:38.820
So even as this old
school style war continues

00:30:38.820 --> 00:30:39.840
to rage in Ukraine,

00:30:39.840 --> 00:30:41.790
we're seeing an evolution
of how conflict works

00:30:41.790 --> 00:30:42.623
in our world.

00:30:42.623 --> 00:30:43.740
Where once a lot of conflict revolved

00:30:43.740 --> 00:30:46.530
around natural resources
like oil, most recently,

00:30:46.530 --> 00:30:47.670
the currency of power.

00:30:47.670 --> 00:30:49.920
We've moved to an era
where a magical piece

00:30:49.920 --> 00:30:52.110
of metal-like substance called silicon,

00:30:52.110 --> 00:30:53.790
pulsing ones and zeros,

00:30:53.790 --> 00:30:56.940
is kind of the new oil,
the new currency of power,

00:30:56.940 --> 00:30:59.160
the new thing that we should protect

00:30:59.160 --> 00:31:01.260
to protect our military supremacy.

00:31:01.260 --> 00:31:03.810
So in a big shift of the
trend of globalization,

00:31:03.810 --> 00:31:06.492
countries are now turning
inward to protect their stuff,

00:31:06.492 --> 00:31:10.127
leading to a new era of
distrust, severed connection,

00:31:10.127 --> 00:31:11.883
and rising tensions.

00:31:13.899 --> 00:31:14.732
Okay.

00:31:16.350 --> 00:31:19.110
Okay, okay, semiconductors is over.

